 and getImage bounds

FlyWeb: Skia 7dc6c0c342 from the branch-heads/8078 roll 848c24c (16a9d4d9a345..7dc6c0c3424a),
applied on the pending Skia tree 32f1340fb3 (after skia/0001). Same patch-id as upstream (38a6e5929e).

Original change's description:
> [SkScalerContext] Harden LCD16 and getImage bounds
>
> When a font scaler retains state across glyph loads, consecutive loads can diverge in outline position and dimensions. In SkScalerContextFTUtils::generateGlyphImage, the kLCD16_Format path previously intersected pixel-space mask.fBounds against FreeType's 3x subpixel-scaled bitmap dimensions and subtracted unscaled pixel offsets from subpixel width, rows, and buffer pointers, triggering subpixel misalignment and assertion failures in copyFT2LCD16.
>
> Convert FreeType's LCD bitmap bounds to pixel coordinates before intersecting with mask.fBounds, validate LCD pixel mode and 3x divisibility, and crop both the subpixel FT_Bitmap and destination SkMask to the pixel overlap. Also guard non-LCD subpixel outline translation against SkFDot6 overflow, assert non-empty in-bounds pre-allocated buffers at SkScalerContext::getImage entry, and add FreeType_GenerateGlyphImageDivergentOutline in tests/FontHostFreeTypeTest.cpp.
>
